# Root .dockerignore — applies to every build that uses `.` as context.
#
# The CodeSeal build context is intentionally narrow:
#   - cli/         Rust source for the sgit binary
#   - portal/      Next.js + workers source (and only source)
#   - infra/docker/  Dockerfiles + config files copied INTO images
#
# Everything else either bloats the daemon push (node_modules, .next,
# target/) or is irrelevant to image builds (docs, scripts, tests).
#
# A bloated context is the single biggest invisible build cost: BuildKit
# has to hash every file to compute the cache key, and `COPY .` would
# silently pull gigabytes of dev artifacts into image layers.

# ── VCS + editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea
.vscode
*.swp

# ── Node.js artifacts (per-tree; the portal-specific .dockerignore
#    catches sub-tree paths, this one catches stray copies) ──────────
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/dist
**/out
**/coverage
**/storybook-static

# ── Rust artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/target

# ── OS / tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Secrets — NEVER ship into an image ────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_ed25519*
**/id_rsa*

# ── Docs + planning + scripts (not used by any image build) ───────────
docs
scripts
data            # local postgres data dir from compose volume mount
infra/k8s
infra/terraform

# ── Test + tooling outputs ────────────────────────────────────────────
**/playwright-report
**/playwright/.cache
**/test-results
**/.vitest-cache
**/junit.xml
**/coverage.xml

# ── Compose-managed bind mounts left behind locally ───────────────────
data/postgres
data/redis
